// spec: LEX-018, EXP-007
//
// An arithmetic result outside the 32-bit range raises rather than wrapping.
//
// ⚠️ This used to be '-2147483648', silently, so a program could compute a
// wrong answer with no sign of it.  Both processors agreed, because the
// interpreter's '+' IS the runtime's -- 'Exit Left + Right' in VisitBinary
// compiles to alg_add.
//
// ⚠️ A build made with -DALG_NO_OVERFLOW_CHECK wraps instead and does NOT
// conform.  The switch exists because the cost is per-operation; it is measured
// at about 2-4% and is off by default in no build the harnesses make.

WriteLn (2147483647 + 1);
